# Consentful plugin — optional environment variables.
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in only what you want. Everything here is
# OPTIONAL; with nothing set the plugin builds and runs exactly the same.

# Optional error reporting for the plugin editor UI (Sentry free tier).
# Leave unset to keep error reporting OFF (default, zero cost, no network).
#
# To enable:
#   1. Create a free Sentry project and copy its DSN.
#   2. Add Sentry's "Loader Script" <script> to plugin/index.html so window.Sentry
#      exists (no npm install required), OR bundle @sentry/browser (see
#      src/lib/errorReporting.ts for the bundled-SDK variant).
#   3. Uncomment and set the DSN below.
#
# VITE_SENTRY_DSN=https://examplePublicKey@o0.ingest.sentry.io/0

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Licensing: no plugin env vars needed.
# Licensing is portal-based — the user pastes a license key and the plugin
# activates the site's published domain against it. The portal API origin and
# publishable key are shared constants in `shared/src/portal.ts`
# (PORTAL_API_BASE / PORTAL_PUBLISHABLE_KEY); set the publishable key there at
# deploy time (tracked in DEPLOY.md §1).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
